# 56x32 desk at 4x authoring density -- the SAME piece as desk.sprite, drawn on a
# grid big enough to hold what 14x8 could not: grain along the boards, a thin
# monitor bezel, readable screen content, individual keycaps, and the key
# light's top edge baked in.
#
# OPTIONAL, and the name is the contract: `<base>@<N>x` declares art authored at
# N times `desk`'s size, so this file must stay exactly 4x `desk.sprite`'s
# dimensions or the painter skips it. The cutaway picks the densest variant whose
# N DIVIDES the render scale — this one at scale 4 (blitted 1:1) or 8 (block-scaled
# the remaining 2x), never at 2. A pack with no variants renders exactly as before.
@frame 0
